# `metadata/` — Validated identity and durable run records

## Authority

The root [`README.md`](../README.md) contract defines this directory's placement
and lifecycle. Root and local [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) files define who may
change factual records.

## Use this directory for

- `schemas.py`: Pydantic schemas for machine-readable project metadata.
- `path_safety.py`: shared no-symlink/no-escape checks used by durable-record
  operator commands.
- `provenance_records.py`: the canonical parser/serializer shared by run
  registration, delivery freezing, and notebook-entry generation.
- Validated manifests mapping stable sample identifiers and conditions to
  catalogued raw files.
- `runs.csv`: the append-only index of deliberately registered executions.
- `provenance/<execution_id>.json`: the immutable complete provenance manifest
  archived when that execution is registered.

{% if include_example %}`samples.example.csv` is a small manifest for the bundled
synthetic fixture. It demonstrates the schema; it is not evidence that a real
sample or acquisition exists.
{% endif %}

Sample manifests selected by the DAG stay under `metadata/`. Every `file` value
is repository-relative and below `data/raw/`; the only placement exception is a
small synthetic input below `tests/fixtures/raw/`. Each real raw entry must have
clean, committed adjacent DVC metadata before DAG construction.

## Lifecycle

The pipeline reads manifests but does not invent them. It may generate current
provenance in `results/provenance.json`; that file becomes durable only when a
person approves run registration. Registration serializes writers, publishes the
immutable archive first, then atomically rewrites the ledger. This is not a
two-file atomic transaction: a retry idempotently completes a safe archive-only
state left by an interrupted ledger write. An execution ID may not silently
acquire different content. Registration rehashes files through no-follow reads,
revalidates the scientific config and both content identities, and requires all
identity-bearing Git/DVC metadata to be committed and unchanged at the recorded
revision.

Keep these small records in Git. Raw and processed payload bytes remain under
`data/` and use DVC according to the root contract.
